Changes of the Raku package "Math::NIntegrate".

0.0.6 2026-10-07
    - Performance related refactoring, ≈ 25% speed-up
    - MonteCarlo strategy improvements: better error handling, processing partitioning and random seed options
    - Implemented Romberg quadrature for TrapezoidalRule
    - Grammar and interpreter enhancements to:
        - Take a list of integers a value for the "partitioning" option
        - Process "romberg-quadrature" option

0.0.5 2026-10-05
    - Fixed a bug in the handling of integrals with range (-Inf, Inf)
    - Implemented max-points stopping criteria for the Global-Adaptive and Local-Adaptive strategies
        - Not working properly yet for MultiDimensionalRule

0.0.4 2026-10-05
    - Streamlined computations with user defined integration rules and strategies
    - Implemented (crude) Monte-Carlo strategy
    - Integrals can have functional boundaries
        - I.e. this works: nintegrate({$^x + $^y}, ['x', 0, 1], ['y', {$^x.sqrt}, {$^x}])

0.0.3 2026-10-02
    - Process user specified "singular points" given in the range specs
      - For example:
      - nintegrate({1/(1-$^x).abs.sqrt}, <x 0 1 2>)
      - nintegrate({1/($^x + $^y).abs.sqrt}, <x -1 0 1>, <y -1 0 1>)
    - Fixes for both concise- and multi-component Cartesian rule specifications
    - Facilitation of stepping away from singular points during integrand evaluation
    - Special representation methods -- gist, Hash, Str -- for strategies and rules

0.0.2 2026-10-01
    - Implemented LocalAdaptive integration strategy
      - Related region division implementation and grammar/interpreter extensions.

0.0.1 2026-09-28
    - First version with:
        - GlobalAdaptive integration strategy
            - Can be given an integration monitor routine as an argument.
        - The integration rules:
            - Cartesian, ClenshawCurtis, GaussKronrod, MonteCarlo, MultiDimensional, NewtonCotes, Trapezoidal
        - Singularity handler by Iri, Moriguti, & Takesawa ("IMT rule").
        - Comprehensive integrator spec parsing and interpretation
        - Kahaner integrator tests
        - CLI script
